.TH fmt_escapecharcontrol 3
.SH NAME
fmt_escapecharcontrol \- escape control characters
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <fmt.h>
.PP
size_t \fBfmt_escapecharcontrol\fR(char *\fIdest\fR, int \fIc\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfmt_escapecharcontrol\fR encodes a character \fIc\fR, applying escape sequences primarily for control characters.
.PP
If \fIc\fR is a printable character (>= 0x20) and not a control character according to \fBiscntrl(3)\fR, the character is copied as-is to \fIdest\fR.
.PP
Control characters or those below 0x20 are escaped. Common escapes like '\n', '\r', and '\t' are mapped to their backslash equivalents (2 bytes). Other non-printable characters are encoded using backslash-prefixed sequences (4 bytes).
.PP
If \fIdest\fR is not NULL, the result is written to \fIdest\fR.
.PP
The function returns the number of bytes required (or written).
.SH SEE ALSO
fmt_escapecharc(3)